          "text": "The pattern indexes as an **orthorhombic C-centered cell**, with the long-axis series \\(020,040,060,\\ldots\\). The best assignment is the **Hf\\(_2\\)AuSi\\(_4\\)/Zr\\(_2\\)CuSi\\(_4\\)-type structure**, space group **Cmcm (No. 63)**, Pearson symbol **oC28**, \\(Z=4\\).\n\nRefined lattice parameters from the peak positions are approximately:\n\n\\[\na=3.6834\\ \\text{\\AA},\\qquad b=32.525\\ \\text{\\AA},\\qquad c=3.6600\\ \\text{\\AA}.\n\\]\n\nThe heavy-atom/prototype assignment is robust. The fractional coordinates below are a prototype-constrained powder solution; the Si coordinates should be regarded as approximate pending a full-profile Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_Hf2AuSi4\n_audit_creation_method              'powder indexing and prototype-constrained structure solution'\n_chemical_name_common               'hafnium gold silicide'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Au Hf2 Si4'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'Hf2AuSi4'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               4\n\n_cell_length_a                       3.6834\n_cell_length_b                      32.5250\n_cell_length_c                       3.6600\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        438.5\n\n_space_group_crystal_system         orthorhombic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'C m c m'\n_space_group_name_Hall              '-C 2c 2'\n_space_group_IT_number              63\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn       10.09\n\n_diffrn_radiation_probe             x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nAu1   Au   4   c   0.0000   0.0815   0.2500   1.000   0.50\nHf1   Hf   8   f   0.0000   0.1590   0.0600   1.000   0.45\nSi1   Si   8   f   0.0000   0.0295   0.6150   1.000   0.60\nSi2   Si   8   f   0.0000   0.2190   0.1150   1.000   0.60\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing supporting this cell is:\n\n| \\(2\\theta_{\\rm obs}\\) | Assignment |\n|---:|:---|\n| 5.43\u00b0 | 020 |\n| 10.87\u00b0 | 040 |\n| 16.33\u00b0 | 060 |\n| 21.84\u00b0 | 080 |\n| 24.30\u00b0 | 110 |\n| 24.89\u00b0 | 021 |\n| 25.52\u00b0 | 130 |\n| 26.66\u00b0 | 041 |\n| 27.39\u00b0 | 0 10 0 |\n| 29.40\u00b0 | 061 |\n| 33.00\u00b0 | 0 12 0 |\n| 35.51\u00b0 | 131 |\n| 37.24\u00b0 | 151 |\n| 38.70\u00b0 | 0 14 0 |\n| 39.72\u00b0 | 171 |\n\nNo distinct alternative Bravais lattice survives the systematic peak-position test. A non-centrosymmetric subgroup such as **Cmc2\\(_1\\)** cannot be rigorously excluded by powder intensities alone, but there is no clear evidence requiring symmetry reduction from the Cmcm prototype.",
